From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] RenderManager: delete the renderer under the locks its users
 hold

CVideoPlayer::CloseFile() uninitialises the render manager before it
stops the player thread, and the player thread closes audio before
video, so the video thread can still be in AddVideoPicture() while
UnInit() runs. UnInit() deleted the renderer holding only m_statelock;
AddVideoPicture() checks and uses it under m_presentlock and
m_datalock, so it could write into a renderer just deleted.

UnInit() now deletes it under both, in the order Configure() and
Flush() take them; AddVideoPicture() then finds no renderer and
returns.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp
index 5c51144338..219fae7ba1 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp
@@ -537,7 +537,12 @@ void CRenderManager::UnInit()
   m_debugRenderer.Dispose();
 
   m_captureBlit.reset();
-  DeleteRenderer();
+  {
+    // the player's video thread may still be in AddVideoPicture() until it is stopped
+    std::unique_lock lock2(m_presentlock);
+    std::unique_lock lock3(m_datalock);
+    DeleteRenderer();
+  }
 
   m_renderState = STATE_UNCONFIGURED;
   m_picture.Reset();
